From 552c1f6000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NXP BSP Team <bsp@nxp.com>
Date: Tue, 20 May 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Remove Intel-specific dead includes not needed on NXP

The headers intel-ipmi-oem/sdrutils.hpp and
phosphor-ipmi-host/selutility.hpp are included unconditionally but
nothing from either header is actually referenced anywhere in
sel_logger.cpp or its included files. Drop both dead includes so the
file compiles without intel-ipmi-oem or phosphor-ipmi-host in the
sysroot (neither package is built for NXP platforms).

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [NXP platform specific]
Signed-off-by: NXP BSP Team <bsp@nxp.com>
---
 src/sel_logger.cpp | 2 --
 1 file changed, 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/sel_logger.cpp b/src/sel_logger.cpp
index 1234567..abcdefg 100644
--- a/src/sel_logger.cpp
+++ b/src/sel_logger.cpp
@@ -19,7 +19,5 @@
 #include <boost/asio/io_context.hpp>
 #include <boost/container/flat_map.hpp>
 #include <boost/container/flat_set.hpp>
-#include <intel-ipmi-oem/sdrutils.hpp>
-#include <phosphor-ipmi-host/selutility.hpp>
 #include <pulse_event_monitor.hpp>
 #include <sdbusplus/asio/object_server.hpp>
